  <sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
    <selectionEntryGroup id="orks-kolo-0000-0001" name="Da Kolours" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true">
      <constraints>
        <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="0" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-kolo-0000-0001-c1" type="min"/>
        <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-kolo-0000-0001-c2" type="max"/>
      </constraints>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry id="orks-kolo-red0-0001" name="Da Kolours (Red)" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-kolo-red0-c1" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile id="orks-kolo-red0-pr01" name="Da Kolours (Red)" hidden="false" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">Red Wunz Go Faster: A unit with Da Kolours (Red) gains +1 to its Movement Characteristic and gains the Light Sub-type. If a model already has the Heavy Sub-type, it instead loses the Heavy Sub-type rather than gaining the Light Sub-type.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="orks-kolo-red0-il01" name="Red Wunz Go Faster" hidden="false" targetId="orks-rule-kolo-red0" type="rule"/>
          </infoLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="orks-kolo-blk0-0001" name="Da Kolours (Black)" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-kolo-blk0-c1" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile id="orks-kolo-blk0-pr01" name="Da Kolours (Black)" hidden="false" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">Black Is Ded 'Ard: When resolving Wounds against a model with Da Kolours (Black) where the Strength of the attack is equal to the Toughness of the target, the Wound roll succeeds only on a roll of 5+ instead of the usual 4+. In addition, when resolving attacks against a Vehicle with Da Kolours (Black), if the AP of the attack exceeds the Armour Value by only 1, the result is a Glancing Hit rather than a Penetrating Hit.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="orks-kolo-blk0-il01" name="Black Is Ded 'Ard" hidden="false" targetId="orks-rule-kolo-blk0" type="rule"/>
          </infoLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="orks-kolo-yel0-0001" name="Da Kolours (Yellow)" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-kolo-yel0-c1" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile id="orks-kolo-yel0-pr01" name="Da Kolours (Yellow)" hidden="false" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">Yellow Goes Bomm: When a model with Da Kolours (Yellow) makes a shooting attack and scores a To Hit roll of 6 (before any modifiers), the Strength of that hit is increased by +1. For weapons with the Blast special rule, if the Scatter dice result is a Direct Hit, the Strength of all hits from that attack is increased by +1.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="orks-kolo-yel0-il01" name="Yellow Goes Bomm" hidden="false" targetId="orks-rule-kolo-yel0" type="rule"/>
          </infoLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="orks-kolo-blu0-0001" name="Da Kolours (Blue)" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-kolo-blu0-c1" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile id="orks-kolo-blu0-pr01" name="Da Kolours (Blue)" hidden="false" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">Blue Gots All Da Luck: Once per phase, a unit with Da Kolours (Blue) may re-roll a single failed To Hit roll, To Wound roll, or Saving Throw.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="orks-kolo-blu0-il01" name="Blue Gots All Da Luck" hidden="false" targetId="orks-rule-kolo-blu0" type="rule"/>
          </infoLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="orks-kolo-wht0-0001" name="Da Kolours (White)" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-kolo-wht0-c1" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile id="orks-kolo-wht0-pr01" name="Da Kolours (White)" hidden="false" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">White Means Deff: When a model with Da Kolours (White) scores a To Wound roll or Armour Penetration roll of 5+, the target suffers a -1 modifier to its Armour Saves and Damage Mitigation rolls against that attack.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="orks-kolo-wht0-il01" name="White Means Deff" hidden="false" targetId="orks-rule-kolo-wht0" type="rule"/>
          </infoLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="orks-kolo-grn0-0001" name="Da Kolours (Green)" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-kolo-grn0-c1" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile id="orks-kolo-grn0-pr01" name="Da Kolours (Green)" hidden="false" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">But Green Is Best: A model with Da Kolours (Green) gains +1 to its Weapon Skill Characteristic when fighting in close combat if there is at least one other friendly unit with Da Kolours (Green) also engaged in close combat within 6&quot;. In addition, models with Da Kolours (Green) gain +1 Strength when resolving Ram and Hammer of Wrath attacks.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="orks-kolo-grn0-il01" name="But Green Is Best" hidden="false" targetId="orks-rule-kolo-grn0" type="rule"/>
          </infoLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="orks-kolo-pur0-0001" name="Da Kolours (Purple)" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-kolo-pur0-c1" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile id="orks-kolo-pur0-pr01" name="Da Kolours (Purple)" hidden="false" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">No Wun's Eva Seen A Purple Ork: When an enemy unit targets a unit with Da Kolours (Purple) with a Shooting Attack, Charge, or Reaction, the effective range for that attack or action is increased by +2&quot;. This means the enemy unit must be 2&quot; closer than normal to be in range.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="orks-kolo-pur0-il01" name="No Wun's Eva Seen A Purple Ork" hidden="false" targetId="orks-rule-kolo-pur0" type="rule"/>
          </infoLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
    <selectionEntryGroup id="orks-wlt0-0000-0001" name="Ork Warlord Traits" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true">
      <constraints>
        <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-wlt0-0000-0001-c1" type="max"/>
        <constraint field="selections" scope="force" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-wlt0-0000-0001-c2" type="max"/>
      </constraints>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry id="orks-wlt0-arch-0001" name="Arch-Tyrant" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-wlt0-arch-c1" type="max"/>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="force" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-wlt0-arch-c2" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile id="orks-wlt0-arch-pr01" name="Arch-Tyrant" hidden="false" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">All friendly units with the Mob Sub-type within 12&quot; of this Warlord gain the Fearless Special Rule. In addition, an army whose Warlord has this Trait may make an additional Reaction during the opposing player's Assault phase so long as the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="orks-wlt0-bles-0001" name="Blessed by Gork (or possibly Mork)" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-wlt0-bles-c1" type="max"/>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="force" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-wlt0-bles-c2" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile id="orks-wlt0-bles-pr01" name="Blessed by Gork (or possibly Mork)" hidden="false" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">At the start of each of the Controlling Player's turns, this Warlord generates 3 Blessing Dice. These dice may be used during the turn to modify any single die roll made by this Warlord or any unit they have joined by +1 or -1 per Blessing Die spent. Unused Blessing Dice are lost at the end of the turn. In addition, an army whose Warlord has this Trait may make an additional Reaction during the opposing player's Assault phase so long as the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="orks-wlt0-thun-0001" name="Like a Thunderbolt" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-wlt0-thun-c1" type="max"/>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="force" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-wlt0-thun-c2" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile id="orks-wlt0-thun-pr01" name="Like a Thunderbolt" hidden="false" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">Whenever this Warlord or the unit they have joined is targeted by a shooting attack during the opposing player's Shooting phase, the unit may immediately move up to 6&quot; directly towards the attacking unit, after the attack has been resolved. This movement does not count as a Charge or trigger Reactions. In addition, an army whose Warlord has this Trait may make an additional Reaction during the opposing player's Assault phase so long as the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="orks-wlt0-brut-0001" name="Brutal (but kunnin')" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-wlt0-brut-c1" type="max"/>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="force" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-wlt0-brut-c2" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile id="orks-wlt0-brut-pr01" name="Brutal (but kunnin')" hidden="false" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">This Warlord gains the Rage (D3+1) and Counter-Attack (D3) Special Rules. In addition, an army whose Warlord has this Trait may make an additional Reaction during the opposing player's Assault phase so long as the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="orks-wlt0-kunn-0001" name="Kunnin' (but brutal)" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-wlt0-kunn-c1" type="max"/>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="force" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-wlt0-kunn-c2" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile id="orks-wlt0-kunn-pr01" name="Kunnin' (but brutal)" hidden="false" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">This Warlord gains the Scouts Special Rule. In addition, for every full 1000 points in the army, the Controlling Player may select one unit with the Troops Force Organisation slot that also gains the Scouts and Outflank Special Rules. These units must be nominated before deployment begins. In addition, an army whose Warlord has this Trait may make an additional Reaction during the opposing player's Assault phase so long as the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="orks-wlt0-best-0001" name="Best of the Beasts" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-wlt0-best-c1" type="max"/>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="force" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-wlt0-best-c2" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile id="orks-wlt0-best-pr01" name="Best of the Beasts" hidden="false" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">This Warlord gains the Battle-Hardened (1) Special Rule. In addition, the Controlling Player may select one unit of Nobz, Meganobz, or Nob Bikerz in the army. That unit gains the Skarboyz upgrade at no additional cost. In addition, an army whose Warlord has this Trait may make an additional Reaction during the opposing player's Assault phase so long as the Warlord has not been removed as a casualty.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
    <selectionEntryGroup id="orks-wagh-0000-0001" name="Waaagh! Armies" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true">
      <constraints>
        <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="orks-wagh-0000-c001" type="max"/>
      </constraints>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry id="orks-wagh-0001-0001" name="Air Waaagh!" page="95" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule id="orks-wagh-0001-r001" name="Air Waaagh!" page="95" hidden="false">
              <description>Effects
• Any unit in a Detachment using this Waaagh! Army that is eligible to take a Trukk as a Dedicated Transport may instead take a Warkopta as a Dedicated Transport.
• All models with the Vehicle Unit Type and the Flyer Sub-type in a Detachment using this Waaagh! Army gain Strafing Run (1) on the turn they arrive from Reserves.
• When resolving a Crashes &amp; Burns result for a model with the Flyer Sub-type from a Detachment using this Waaagh! Army, the controlling player may re-roll the scatter dice.
Limitations
• The Warlord of an army using this Waaagh! Army must be an Ork Baron with the Waaagh! special rule.
• A Detachment using this Waaagh! Army must include more units with the Flyer Sub-type than Troops choices.
• A Detachment using this Waaagh! Army may not include any Heavy Support or Lords of War choices that do not have the Flyer Sub-type.

^Manually check restrictions and limitations against source (Xenologica 2e p95)</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="orks-wagh-0002-0001" name="Beast Snaggin&apos; Waaagh!" page="95" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule id="orks-wagh-0002-r001" name="Beast Snaggin&apos; Waaagh!" page="95" hidden="false">
              <description>Effects
• All models in a Detachment using this Waaagh! Army with the Monster Hunter special rule may re-roll failed To Wound rolls against models with the Gargantuan or Super-Heavy Sub-types.
• Any Wildboyz unit with 10 or fewer models in a Detachment using this Waaagh! Army may take a Kill Rig as a Dedicated Transport.
Limitations
• The Warlord of an army using this Waaagh! Army must be a Wildboss with the Waaagh! special rule.
• An army using this Waaagh! Army must include at least one Weirdboy or Weirdboss.
• A Detachment using this Waaagh! Army must include more units with the Monstrous Creature Unit Type than units with the Vehicle or Dreadnought Unit Types.

^Manually check restrictions and limitations against source (Xenologica 2e p95–96)</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="orks-wagh-0003-0001" name="Da &apos;Ardest Waaagh!" page="96" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule id="orks-wagh-0003-r001" name="Da &apos;Ardest Waaagh!" page="96" hidden="false">
              <description>Effects
• Meganobz units may be taken as Troops choices in a Detachment using this Waaagh! Army.
• Any Meganobz unit with 3 or fewer models in a Detachment using this Waaagh! Army may take a Gorkanaut or Morkanaut as a Dedicated Transport.
• A Detachment using this Waaagh! Army gains +2 additional Elites slots, which may only be used for Nobz, Meganobz or Bikers units.
Limitations
• The Warlord of an army using this Waaagh! Army must be a Megaboss or Ghazghkull.
• A Detachment using this Waaagh! Army may include a maximum of 1 Fast Attack choice and 1 Heavy Support choice.

^Manually check restrictions and limitations against source (Xenologica 2e p96)</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="orks-wagh-0004-0001" name="Da Green Tide" page="96" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule id="orks-wagh-0004-r001" name="Da Green Tide" page="96" hidden="false">
              <description>Effects
• All Boyz Wave and Unwashed Hordes units in a Detachment using this Waaagh! Army gain the Unending Horde (4+) special rule.
• Units in a Detachment using this Waaagh! Army that declare a Charge targeting a unit that is already the target of a Charge by another friendly unit in the same Phase are not considered Disordered.
• Units from a Detachment using this Waaagh! Army that are placed into Reserves may enter play from any table edge when they arrive from Reserves.
• A Detachment using this Waaagh! Army gains +2 additional Compulsory Troops slots, which may only be filled by Boyz Wave units.
Limitations
• All Compulsory Troops choices in a Detachment using this Waaagh! Army must be Boyz Wave or Unwashed Hordes units.

^Manually check restrictions and limitations against source (Xenologica 2e p96–97)</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
